WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.569
-Today, Senators reviewed
the FBI report

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:04.603
on the allegations against

00:00:04.603 --> 00:00:06.139
Supreme Court nominee
Brett Kavanaugh,

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:07.406
despite the fact that the FBI

00:00:07.406 --> 00:00:09.775
didn't actually conduct
a serious investigation.

00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:12.045
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:16.282
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:19.052
When the allegations against
Kavanaugh first surfaced,

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:20.853
Trump's aides
tried to restrain him.

00:00:20.853 --> 00:00:22.688
But to literally
no one's surprise,

00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:24.624
that facade quickly unraveled.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:25.959
And in the last week or so,

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:28.128
he's had one outburst
after another.

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:31.330
-If we brought
George Washington here

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:33.366
and we said,
"We have George Washington,"

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.101
the Democrats
would vote against him.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.537
I'm a very famous person,
unfortunately.

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:39.738
"This is so-and-so calling."
He took the call.

00:00:39.738 --> 00:00:41.708
Why is he taking a call
from a Russian?

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:42.942
-I'd like to turn
to Judge Kavanaugh --

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:43.943
-Don't do that.
Don't do that.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.144
Do you have --
-Mr. President --

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:46.212
-Excuse me.
Go ahead, please.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:47.547
-Just to wrap up,
can you promise to --

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:48.915
-You know what?
You've really had enough.

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:50.116
Hey, you've had enough.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.517
I'm not a drinker.

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:54.153
I can honestly say
I never had a beer in my life.

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:55.688
I've never had alcohol.

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.690
You know, for whatever reason.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.292
Can you imagine if I had?

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:00.860
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:04.364
I honestly --
I honestly can't.

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:06.165
You already scream and yell

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:08.901
and slur your words
like a stumbling drunk.

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:12.071
Even the way you stand is
the way a drunk guy would stand

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:14.273
if he was trying to pretend
he wasn't drunk.

00:01:14.273 --> 00:01:16.642
"Okay.
Just act cool."

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:17.943
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:01:17.943 --> 00:01:20.246
"Arms at your side.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:23.449
Puff out your chest.
No one --

00:01:23.449 --> 00:01:26.352
No -- No one will notice
you're swaying back and forth.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:29.589
Oh.
Oh, my God, I'm gonna puke."

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:31.157
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.459
The president mocked
and dismissed the allegations

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:35.394
against Kavanaugh,
so it's no wonder

00:01:35.394 --> 00:01:37.463
that the FBI investigation
he requested

00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:39.899
wasn't actually a serious
attempt to get at the truth.

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:42.602
Today, for example, the FBI
finally delivered its report,

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.537
and if you're wondering
how that's possible,

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:47.973
it's because their investigation
lasted less than a week.

00:01:47.973 --> 00:01:50.777
They delivered the report
in under a week.

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:53.212
I had to do a report
on the Louisiana Purchase

00:01:53.212 --> 00:01:55.381
in 6th grade,
and it took me a month.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.516
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:59.318
And I got a "C."

00:01:59.318 --> 00:02:01.020
They didn't even
interview Kavanaugh

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.489
or Dr. Christine Blasey Ford.

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:06.259
They really went over this thing
with a no-toothed comb.

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:07.727
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:08.861
And when they were investigating

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:10.329
the other allegations
against Kavanaugh,

00:02:10.329 --> 00:02:11.764
they made it clear
they had no intention

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:14.300
of actually talking to people
who might have more information.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.568
-Deborah Ramirez,
who talked to the FBI

00:02:16.568 --> 00:02:19.172
for two hours about her
allegations of misconduct

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:20.440
when they were at Yale.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:23.175
Ramirez's lawyer says
his client provided a list

00:02:23.175 --> 00:02:24.877
of more than 20 witnesses

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:27.713
who say they could
corroborate her story.

00:02:27.713 --> 00:02:31.016
He says the FBI has not
reached out to any of them.

00:02:31.016 --> 00:02:33.419
-Think about that --
more than 20 people

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:35.288
said they might have
corroborating evidence,

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:37.123
and the FBI
talked to none of them.

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:39.458
If the FBI worked like this
on the "The X-Files,"

00:02:39.458 --> 00:02:41.427
Mulder's landlord
could've been an alien,

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:42.762
and he never would've noticed.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:44.464
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:46.565
In fact, people who said
they could corroborate

00:02:46.565 --> 00:02:47.966
the allegations
against Kavanaugh

00:02:47.966 --> 00:02:50.236
actually tried
to seek out the FBI themselves,

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:51.905
and even then,
they were ignored.

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:53.473
One person
who told "The New Yorker,"

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:54.974
"I can corroborate
Debbie's account,"

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:56.375
reached out to the Bureau
last weekend

00:02:56.375 --> 00:02:57.476
but did not hear back.

00:02:57.476 --> 00:02:59.378
Frustrated,
he submitted his statement

00:02:59.378 --> 00:03:00.914
through an FBI web portal.

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:05.852
No one should ever have to
log on to the FBI's web portal.

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.653
You shouldn't have
to contact the FBI

00:03:07.653 --> 00:03:10.356
the same way I pay my dentist.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:12.558
In fact, no one should ever
have to log on to anything

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:14.527
that's still called
a web portal.

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.328
"Would you like to report
a crime to the FBI?

00:03:16.328 --> 00:03:18.698
Begin by logging on
to the information superhighway

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:20.500
and popping in your AOL CD-ROM."

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.401
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.401 --> 00:03:24.370
This investigation
was obviously a sham,

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.305
and sure enough, when the report
finally came in today,

00:03:26.305 --> 00:03:28.708
Republican Senators
like Jeff Flake and Orrin Hatch

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:31.277
were quick to claim that
there was nothing new in it.

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:34.213
-The Senate Judiciary Committee
chairman Chuck Grassley saying,

00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:36.449
"There's nothing
we didn't already know,"

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:39.318
and that there was
"no hint of misconduct."

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:41.687
Senator Jeff Flake
says he has seen,

00:03:41.687 --> 00:03:44.223
"No additional
corroborating information"

00:03:44.223 --> 00:03:45.892
against Judge Kavanaugh.

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:48.160
-No corroboration.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:51.431
No confirmation of any
of these outrageous accusations

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:53.666
that have been made against him.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:55.368
-We have found nothing.

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:57.436
Absolutely nothing
to corroborate

00:03:57.436 --> 00:03:59.271
accusations against him.

00:03:59.271 --> 00:04:01.841
-That's because
you didn't look for it.

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:03.475
You guys
are like treasure hunters

00:04:03.475 --> 00:04:06.779
who decided to call it quits
before you flipped over the map.

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:08.247
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:10.649
This entire process
has been a deeply revealing look

00:04:10.649 --> 00:04:11.718
at Senate Republicans.

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:13.352
Trump, of course,
has always been unhinged,

00:04:13.352 --> 00:04:15.787
but Republicans in the Senate
like to pretend

00:04:15.787 --> 00:04:18.958
that they were all the stable,
above-it-all statesmen

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:20.759
who were just putting up
with his antics

00:04:20.759 --> 00:04:22.361
to get their judges
and tax cuts.

00:04:22.361 --> 00:04:24.097
But over the last few weeks,
many of them

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:26.532
have lost their minds
in Trumpian fashion.

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:28.734
Just take South Carolina Senator
Lindsey Graham.

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:30.569
Graham was once thought of
as a Trump critic,

00:04:30.569 --> 00:04:33.839
but then, during the Kavanaugh
hearing, he exploded with rage.

00:04:33.839 --> 00:04:37.810
-I cannot imagine what you and
your family have gone through.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.011
Boy, you all want power.

00:04:39.011 --> 00:04:40.712
God, I hope you never get it.

00:04:40.712 --> 00:04:43.683
I hope the American people
can see through this sham.

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:47.387
God, I hate to say it, 'cause
these have been my friends.

00:04:47.387 --> 00:04:50.689
But let me tell you,
when it comes to this,

00:04:50.689 --> 00:04:53.025
you're looking
for a fair process,

00:04:53.025 --> 00:04:57.230
you came to the wrong town
at the wrong time, my friend.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.965
-He sounds like
an outlaw gunslinger

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:01.167
threatening to kill
the Lone Ranger.

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:02.669
But let's face it,

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:04.737
if it came down
to an Old West gunfight,

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:07.339
Graham would be the guy
hiding behind the pickle barrel

00:05:07.339 --> 00:05:08.875
with his fingers in his ears.

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:10.609
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.609 --> 00:05:12.345
He did the same thing yesterday
when he was asked

00:05:12.345 --> 00:05:14.780
about the President
viciously mocking Dr. Ford.

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:16.782
This time, Graham was in front
of an audience,

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:17.916
and they booed him.

00:05:17.916 --> 00:05:20.186
-I don't like what the President
said last night.

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:24.424
I'm the first person to say
I want to hear from Dr. Ford.

00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:27.493
I thought
she was handled respectfully.

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:30.663
I thought Kavanaugh
was treated like crap.

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:31.663
[ Audience booing, hissing ]

00:05:31.663 --> 00:05:33.533
Yeah, well, boo yourself.

00:05:33.533 --> 00:05:35.301
-Man...
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:38.003
...he's just fighting
with the audience now.

00:05:38.003 --> 00:05:41.874
He's like the least-threatening
pro wrestler ever.

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:44.043
"My name's Lindsey,
but you can call me

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:45.978
the Southern Snake,
and, brother,

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:48.013
I'm gonna bite your ankle."

00:05:48.013 --> 00:05:51.317
[ Audience booing ]

00:05:51.317 --> 00:05:53.318
"Well, boo right back at you!

00:05:53.318 --> 00:05:55.021
You're all a bunch of meanies!"

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:59.391
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.391 --> 00:06:01.393
Graham has gone
so far off the deep end

00:06:01.393 --> 00:06:03.462
that he even called
for one of his colleagues,

00:06:03.462 --> 00:06:06.832
Minnesota Senator Amy Klobuchar,
to apologize to Kavanaugh.

00:06:06.832 --> 00:06:08.534
You might remember
these exchanges

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.670
from the hearing last week
in which a furious Kavanaugh

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:12.605
tried to turn questions
about his hard-drinking

00:06:12.605 --> 00:06:14.073
high school and college days

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:15.975
back on the Senators
asking them.

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:17.343
-I like beer.
I like beer.

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:19.578
I don't know if you --
You like beer, Senator, or not?

00:06:19.578 --> 00:06:20.812
-Um...
-What do you like to drink?

00:06:20.812 --> 00:06:21.881
-Next one is --

00:06:21.881 --> 00:06:23.482
-Senator, what do you
like to drink?

00:06:23.482 --> 00:06:25.317
-So, you're saying
there's never been a case

00:06:25.317 --> 00:06:28.153
where you drank so much
that you didn't remember

00:06:28.153 --> 00:06:30.523
what happened the night before
or part of what happened?

00:06:30.523 --> 00:06:35.861
-You're asking about blackout.
I don't know. Have you?

00:06:35.861 --> 00:06:38.497
-Could you answer the question,
Judge, and just --

00:06:38.497 --> 00:06:42.368
So, you -- that's not happened?
Is that your answer?

00:06:42.368 --> 00:06:45.270
-Yeah.
And I'm curious if you have.

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:46.973
-I have no drinking problem,
Judge.

00:06:46.973 --> 00:06:48.241
-Yeah, nor do I.

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:49.542
-Ugh!

00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:51.744
We all knew this [bleep]
in college, right?

00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:53.679
The guy who would get pulled
over, and the cop would say,

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:55.248
"Do you know how fast
you were going?"

00:06:55.248 --> 00:06:57.917
and this guy would go, "Do you
know how fast I was going?"

00:06:57.917 --> 00:06:59.352
[ Laughter ]

00:06:59.352 --> 00:07:02.154
And then, 20 years later, you
get a LinkedIn request from him,

00:07:02.154 --> 00:07:04.657 line:0%
and he's the CEO
of a dog-poison company.

00:07:04.657 --> 00:07:12.064 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:14.500
The only way he could've looked
crazier during that hearing

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:17.069
is if he was wearing one of
those beer-guzzler helmets.

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:19.272
[ Laughter ]

00:07:19.272 --> 00:07:21.373
No, even Kavanaugh,
as unhinged as he was,

00:07:21.373 --> 00:07:23.943
came back after the break
and apologized to Klobuchar,

00:07:23.943 --> 00:07:26.245
who has written extensively
about her father's alcoholism.

00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:27.579
Yet on Fox News this week,

00:07:27.579 --> 00:07:29.148
Graham said
it was actually Klobuchar

00:07:29.148 --> 00:07:31.149
who owed Kavanaugh an apology.

00:07:31.149 --> 00:07:34.086
-Here's what I think.
Amy Klobuchar should apologize

00:07:34.086 --> 00:07:36.455
to Judge Kavanaugh
and his family

00:07:36.455 --> 00:07:39.692
for being part of a "schmear"
campaign I haven't seen

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:41.727
in over 20 years in politics.

00:07:41.727 --> 00:07:43.729
-Excuse me. Did you say
a "schmear" campaign?

00:07:43.729 --> 00:07:45.397
[ Laughter ]

00:07:45.397 --> 00:07:47.200
Were you hungry
when you did that interview?

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:48.867
Did you just come from the deli?

00:07:48.867 --> 00:07:50.536
"This is a schmear campaign."

00:07:50.536 --> 00:07:51.704
[ Laughter ]

00:07:51.704 --> 00:07:54.173
And as for Hillary,
we should lox her up."

00:07:54.173 --> 00:07:56.108
[ Laughter ]

00:07:56.108 --> 00:07:57.543
"I've had --"

00:07:57.543 --> 00:08:04.717
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:04.717 --> 00:08:06.886
"I've had enough of her capers."

00:08:06.886 --> 00:08:15.427
[ Laughter ]

00:08:15.427 --> 00:08:16.762
Boooooo!

00:08:16.762 --> 00:08:17.897
[ Audience booing ]

00:08:17.897 --> 00:08:22.534
"Boo! You didn't like
my capers joke?!"

00:08:22.534 --> 00:08:25.571
But that clip is such a perfect
microcosm of this entire ordeal.

00:08:25.571 --> 00:08:27.339
Entitled, powerful men
think everyone else

00:08:27.339 --> 00:08:29.642
owes them an apology
for having the audacity

00:08:29.642 --> 00:08:31.409
to held them accountable
for their actions.

00:08:31.409 --> 00:08:34.113
They think that being born
to elite status in society

00:08:34.113 --> 00:08:36.181
means you earned that status,

00:08:36.181 --> 00:08:38.284
and they're furious
at any attempt to take it away.

00:08:38.284 --> 00:08:40.086
That's why Trump
keeps bringing up the fact

00:08:40.086 --> 00:08:41.353
that Kavanaugh went to Yale,

00:08:41.353 --> 00:08:43.288
although he doesn't always
have his facts right.

00:08:43.288 --> 00:08:45.958
-You know, he said that really
what he was focused on

00:08:45.958 --> 00:08:48.827
was trying to be number one
in the class at Yale.

00:08:48.827 --> 00:08:50.395
To me, that was so believable.

00:08:50.395 --> 00:08:52.164
I understand college very well,

00:08:52.164 --> 00:08:55.100
and I understand
being number-one in your class,

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:57.002
and I understand
a lot of things.

00:08:57.002 --> 00:08:59.371
I think he was number one
in his class at Yale.

00:08:59.371 --> 00:09:01.974
He was number one
in his law school at Yale.

00:09:01.974 --> 00:09:04.176
He was, I believe,
number one at Yale.

00:09:04.176 --> 00:09:05.444
Is that a correct statement?

00:09:05.444 --> 00:09:06.712
-No, it's not.

00:09:06.712 --> 00:09:08.748
[ Laughter ]

00:09:12.918 --> 00:09:18.524
And I have to say,
as a favor,

00:09:18.524 --> 00:09:21.193
you should probably
steer clear of asking,

00:09:21.193 --> 00:09:23.595
"Is that a correct statement?"
when you're talking.

00:09:23.595 --> 00:09:25.731
For one, we know you don't care
what the answer is.

00:09:25.731 --> 00:09:27.599
And, also,
it would really slow down

00:09:27.599 --> 00:09:29.234
the momentum at your rallies.

00:09:29.234 --> 00:09:32.204
"We've accomplished more
than any administration ever.

00:09:32.204 --> 00:09:33.739
Is that a correct statement?"
[ Laughter ]

00:09:33.739 --> 00:09:34.940
"It's not?

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:37.376
What about the one before it?
Not that, either?

00:09:37.376 --> 00:09:39.979
Have any of them been correct?
Not one?

00:09:39.979 --> 00:09:42.047
What about when I said it's
great to be in West Virginia?

00:09:42.047 --> 00:09:43.215
This is Mississippi?"

00:09:43.215 --> 00:09:45.350
[ Laughter ]

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:47.553
-Also, can we go back
to this for a second?

00:09:47.553 --> 00:09:49.254
-I understand college very well.

00:09:49.254 --> 00:09:50.756
-"I understand college
very well."

00:09:50.756 --> 00:09:52.959
Sounds like something Jack Black
would say in a movie

00:09:52.959 --> 00:09:56.562
about a bunch of middle-aged
dudes who try to join a frat.

00:09:56.562 --> 00:09:58.931
"I understand college,
and if we're gonna fit in,

00:09:58.931 --> 00:10:01.900
we have go to parties and scream
at the top of our lungs..."

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:03.268
-I like beer.

00:10:03.268 --> 00:10:05.003
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:05.003 --> 00:10:06.839
-What we
are witnessing right now

00:10:06.839 --> 00:10:08.974
is a cultural struggle
over how power works.

00:10:08.974 --> 00:10:10.710
There's a set
of privileged people

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:12.411
who are accustomed
to being insulated

00:10:12.411 --> 00:10:14.112
from the consequences
of their actions

00:10:14.112 --> 00:10:15.347
